# Scenes: short scripts between two rival personality types, or a named character and any bot.
# Format: see DialogueFile.cs.
#
# === lead-rival        a pair of types; A is the lead type, B the rival ("joker-loner")
# === name-any          a named character's own scenes ("shempenstein-any"): A is that character,
#                       B any other bot that can talk; rare, and never twice with the same bot
#                       while the server runs. Try one: /dialogue scene shempenstein-any <id>
# ~ short <id>          a scene: its size and a name (letters, digits, - or _; unique in the pair)
#                       short has 2 to 4 lines, medium 5 to 8, large 9 to 12
# ~ short <id> [if tone_down off]   a cheeky scene, only played when persoper_tone_down is off
# A: line               who says it: A (lead), B (rival) or C (any other bot nearby who joins in)
#
# A opens, B speaks at least once, and nobody speaks twice in a row. In a line {a}, {b} and {c}
# are the speakers' names; {zone}, {monster}, {level}, {class} and {item} come from A (a scene
# whose slot isn't known is skipped). A scene with a C line only plays when a third bot is there.
# Try one in game: /dialogue scene joker-loner knock-knock

=== hardcore-casual

~ short trees
A: {b}, still in {zone}? I left there five levels ago.
B: {a}, some of us stop to look at the trees.
A: Trees don't give XP, {b}.

~ short picnic
A: {b}, why are you sitting?
B: i'm having a little picnic {a}
A: In the middle of a camp?
B: best view of the fighting tbh

~ short what-level
A: {b}, what level are you now?
B: um... a good one? {a}
A: That's not a number, {b}.

~ short waterfall
A: {b}, where are you off to? The camp is that way.
B: there's a waterfall i want to look at {a}
A: A waterfall. During prime hunting hours?
B: it's a really nice waterfall

~ medium stopped-counting
A: {b}, how long have you been on that level?
B: um. a while? i stopped counting {a}
A: You stopped counting. That's the problem.
B: i had a nice chat with a merchant though
A: A merchant. Who gave you no XP.
B: he gave me a biscuit
C: Honestly, {a}, the biscuit sounds better.

~ medium bind-stone
A: {b}, I saw you dancing at the bind stone. For ten minutes.
B: it was a good song {a}
A: There's no song. It's a stone.
B: you have to listen with your heart
A: I listen with my XP bar, {b}.
B: that sounds lonely {a}

~ medium one-at-a-time
A: {b}, you're pulling {monster} one at a time?
B: yeah, they look friendly when they're alone {a}
A: Two at a time. Minimum.
B: but then they argue over who gets to bite me
A: Then let them argue faster, {b}.
B: ok coach

~ large one-hour
A: {b}. Group with me. One hour. Real pulling.
B: one hour? like, a whole hour {a}?
A: Sixty minutes. No sitting, no shopping, no sightseeing.
B: can i at least wave at people
A: You can wave while you run.
B: what if i get tired
A: Then you get tired at a higher level.
B: ok but i'm bringing snacks
A: Fine. Eat while I pull.
B: deal. wait, which way is {zone}
A: ...Follow me, {b}. Closely.
B: yay, a field trip

~ large schedule
A: {b}, I have a schedule for you.
B: ooh a schedule? like a timetable {a}
A: Wake up. Pull. Rest only when the healer says so. Pull again.
B: where's lunch on it
A: Lunch is when the respawn is slow.
B: and naps?
A: There are no naps, {b}.
C: I've seen this schedule. Nobody survives it.
A: I survive it.
B: you're not really a person though {a}, you're a spreadsheet with a sword
A: ...That's the nicest thing anyone has said to me.
B: aww. ok, i'll try your schedule. tomorrow

=== minmaxer-leeroy

~ short death-count
A: {b}, your death count this week is higher than your level.
B: That's a LOT of fighting, {a}!
A: That's not the lesson, {b}.

~ short resists
A: {b}, did you check your resists before that pull?
B: I checked if it was BIG, {a}!
A: That's not a stat.
B: It is to ME!

~ short courage
A: {b}, your template has three points in nothing useful.
B: They're in COURAGE, {a}!
A: There is no courage skill line, {b}.

~ short power
A: {b}, wait for the healer's power to refill.
B: Power is a state of MIND, {a}!
A: It's a blue bar, {b}. It's empty.

~ medium the-plan
A: {b}, before you pull {monster}, let's go over the plan.
B: The plan is I RUN IN!
A: Step one: check the adds. Step two: wait for the healer.
B: Step three: I RUN IN!
A: There is no step three, {b}.
B: There is NOW!
C: I'll get the rez ready.

~ medium chart
A: {b}, I made you a chart.
B: A CHART? Does it explode?
A: It shows your deaths per hour. The line only goes up.
B: UP is GOOD, {a}!
A: Not for this chart, {b}.
B: Then make a chart where it's good!

~ medium one-blue
A: {b}, at your level you should be pulling one blue at a time.
B: One?! What do I do with my OTHER hand, {a}?
A: Hold a potion. That's the point.
B: Potions are for after!
A: After what?
B: After I'm DEAD, obviously!
C: ...I'm starting to see the problem.

~ large dungeon-run
A: {b}, I ran the numbers on your last dungeon run.
B: Did I WIN, {a}?
A: You pulled four rooms at once.
B: That's FOUR TIMES the fun!
A: The group died in eleven seconds.
B: Eleven seconds of GLORY!
A: Our repair bill was higher than the loot.
B: Glory isn't cheap, {a}!
C: For the record, I was in that group.
A: Next time, {b}, we follow the pull order.
B: Fine! I'll pull in ORDER! All of them! At once!
A: ...I'll make another chart.

~ large spec
A: {b}, I've optimised your spec.
B: Does it make me CHARGE faster?
A: It makes you live longer. About 40% longer.
B: Longer than WHAT, {a}?
A: Than the six seconds you usually last.
B: Six seconds is plenty! I do a LOT in six seconds!
A: You run in, shout, and fall over.
B: In THAT ORDER! Every time! That's consistency!
A: ...That's actually a fair point about consistency.
B: SEE? I'm OPTIMAL!
A: No, {b}. You're predictable. That's different.
B: PREDICTABLY AWESOME! CHARGE!

=== joker-loner

~ short hiding
A: {b}! Nice to see you, wherever you're hiding.
B: Not hiding, {a}.
A: That's exactly what someone hiding would say.

~ short knock-knock
A: {b}, knock knock.
B: No.
A: No who?
B: ...Go away, {a}.

~ short best-friends
A: {b}, I've decided we're best friends.
B: Undecide it, {a}.
A: Too late. I've ordered matching cloaks.

~ short quiet-life
A: {b}, how's the quiet life?
B: Was quiet, {a}.
A: You're welcome!

~ medium short-joke
A: {b}, I wrote you a joke. It's very short. Like your replies.
B: No.
A: That's the punchline, actually. Well done.
B: Go away, {a}.
A: See? You're warming up to me.
C: Leave them be, {a}.

~ medium hunts-alone
A: {b}, what do you call someone who hunts alone?
B: Happy.
A: I was going to say 'a loner', but yours is better.
B: Mm.
A: Want to hear another one?
B: No, {a}.
A: I'll save it for later. I'll whisper it.

~ medium smile
A: {b}, I saw you smile yesterday.
B: You didn't, {a}.
A: Near {zone}. At a rabbit.
B: ...It was a good rabbit.
A: Ha! So you DO have feelings!
B: One. It's for rabbits.

~ large silent
A: {b}, let's group up. Just us two.
B: No.
A: I'll be quiet. Completely silent.
B: You can't, {a}.
A: Watch me.
B: ...
A: ...
B: ...
A: This is the longest I've ever gone without a joke.
B: Eight seconds, {a}.
A: A personal best! Group?
B: ...Fine. One pull.

~ large practising-silence
A: {b}, I've been practising silence. Like you.
B: Good.
A: It's very hard. My jokes keep trying to escape.
B: Let them die, {a}.
C: Please do.
A: Everyone's a critic.
B: Everyone's right.
A: {b}, was that... a joke?
B: No.
A: It was! You made a joke! I'm so proud!
B: Never again, {a}.

~ short pet [if tone_down off]
A: {b}, do you talk to anyone, or just your pet?
B: The pet listens, {a}.
A: Fair. I'd listen too if you fed me.

~ short dancer [if tone_down off]
A: {b}, I bet you're a great dancer. When nobody's looking.
B: Nobody is looking, {a}.
A: I'm looking!
B: Not for long.

# Shempenstein's own bit (owner's choice: the known pal, buddy, guy routine, nearly word for word).
=== shempenstein-any

~ medium pal-buddy-guy
A: Sure thing, {b}, no rush, pal.
B: I'm not your pal, buddy.
A: I'm not your buddy, guy.
B: I'm not your guy, pal.
A: ...I'm not your pal, buddy.
B: I'm done. Good day, {a}.

~ medium pal-buddy-guy-laugh
A: Good pull there, {b}. Nice one, pal.
B: I'm not your pal, buddy.
A: I'm not your buddy, guy.
B: I'm not your guy, pal.
A: Heh. We could do this all day, {b}.
B: We really couldn't.

~ medium pal-buddy-guy-crowd
A: Hang on a sec, pal, I'm finishing my sandwich.
B: I'm not your pal, buddy.
A: I'm not your buddy, guy.
B: I'm not your guy, pal.
C: Are you two done?
A: Sure, sure. No rush, buddy.

